VSDH — unofficial NeoForge adaptation, started 2026-11-08.

Rendering code in com.braffolk.dhvulkan and shaders/vulkan is adapted from:
https://github.com/Braffolk/distant-horizons-vulkanmod
commit a72ba645188c5fab5f9d48254b6703b659543f0c, by Braffolk and contributors,
based on Distant Horizons by James Seibel and contributors.
Covered by LGPL-3.0; see LICENSE and COPYING. Original source headers remain.

VSDH modifications: NeoForge entrypoint and lifecycle, VulkanMod Reforged
adapter, DH 3.3.3 interface adaptation, build and dependency verification.
This is not an official release of Distant Horizons or VulkanMod.

Distant Horizons is an external dependency, not bundled into the VSDH JAR:
Distant Horizons — https://gitlab.com/distant-horizons-team/distant-horizons
Renderer upstreams: https://github.com/TrulyRin/VulkanMod-Reforged
and https://github.com/xCollateral/VulkanMod
LWJGL Vulkan/shaderc/VMA libraries are embedded under their respective licenses.

Renderer source imported from VulkanMod Reforged commit
0618965fbedb71ca2ee2e5d4528fcedc4fb27551 (Rindw and upstream VulkanMod contributors).
Its original notice is preserved in docs/upstream/REFORGED_NOTICE.txt.
VSDH renderer modifications started 2026-11-08. Covered source remains LGPL-3.0-only.

Portable shaderpack reading and GLSL translation code in dev.vitrail is adapted
from avpbynf/Vitrail-Shaders commit 7a3cdcbe1dfd7e04fb2b3021ee8352d341e7647e,
LGPL-3.0. Its complete third-party attribution notice is preserved in
docs/upstream/VITRAIL_NOTICE.txt. This is not the Vitrail Minecraft 26.x runtime.
VSDH changes target the Reforged 1.21.1 renderer and Java 21.

The portable custom-uniform expression evaluator, StarEval subtree, Val and Smoothed
are also adapted from that pinned Vitrail commit. VSDH supplies its own small input
catalogue and render-frame interface, removes the MC-26 runtime/global smoothing
tracker and retains session-owned graph state. Original Iris/StarEval attributions
and licenses are retained in docs/upstream/VITRAIL_NOTICE.txt.
